#  The following .env files are available:
# `.env`: Default.
# `.env.local`: Local overrides. **This file is loaded for all environments except test.**
# `.env.development`, `.env.test`, `.env.production`: Environment-specific settings.
# `.env.development.local`, `.env.test.local`, `.env.production.local`: Local overrides of environment-specific settings.

## Development settings.
# The API key to use to fetch information from Warcraft Logs. You need to enter your own API key by creating a new file in the root repo called `.env.local` with the contents: `VITE_WCL_API_KEY=INSERT_YOUR_API_KEY_HERE`. After saving this file, you need to restart `pnpm run start`.
# Do not set the key here!
VITE_WCL_API_KEY=
# The server to use. CN fork: always a relative path (same-origin); WCL API goes
# direct to VITE_WCL_API_BASE or through the /wcl-api/ proxy. There is no fallback
# to wowanalyzer.com: makeWclApiUrl throws when neither WCL variable is configured.
VITE_SERVER_BASE=/
# `true` will force-enable premium status while `false` will force-disable premium status. Any other value will cause the app to check the user data.
VITE_FORCE_PREMIUM=
# CN fork: `true` disables requests that require the wowanalyzer.com backend (user
# session, character profiles outside CN, guild reports, spell info lookups,
# server metrics). Unset means ENABLED (fail-open) — every shipped .env.* sets
# it to true, and deployment configs must too. Related UI entries are hidden.
VITE_DISABLE_USER_FETCH=
VITE_DISABLE_SOCIAL_FEATURES=

## Application settings.
# The path on the server to our (internal) API.
# CN fork: legacy upstream API path. With VITE_DISABLE_SOCIAL_FEATURES=true (all
# shipped configs) nothing requests it; spell-info lookups and server metrics
# are the only remaining consumers and both are gated on that flag.
VITE_API_BASE=i/
# The Sentry DSN can be changed to send errors to a different Sentry project.
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=
# The name of the current environment. This gets set during the production build and is used to separate branches which determine where things get deployed.
VITE_ENVIRONMENT_NAME=
# The version deployed. This gets set during the production build and is used to determine problematic commits.
VITE_VERSION=
# Enable Google Analytics tracking
VITE_ENABLE_GA=false
